1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,680
Quentin Tarantino, one of the most acclaimed filmmakers of all time,

2
00:00:03,680 --> 00:00:08,720
known for bringing his bold ideas to life with surreal visuals and mind-bending storytelling.

3
00:00:08,720 --> 00:00:10,880
But he wasn't always a Hollywood icon.

4
00:00:10,880 --> 00:00:14,160
Once he was just an ordinary guy working at a video store.

5
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:17,280
Until one night he decided to rewrite his story.

6
00:00:17,280 --> 00:00:18,560
And there was like one night...

7
00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:22,080
Stay up all night long and rather than give myself excuses,

8
00:00:22,080 --> 00:00:27,040
I would look at everything that I'm up in my life or everything I'm not doing or whatever

9
00:00:27,040 --> 00:00:48,640
Today I present you the Tarantino Method. To follow this process you'll need three things.

10
00:00:48,640 --> 00:00:53,840
A pen, a notepad, and the dead of night. When the world is silent and now the soul is awake.

11
00:00:53,840 --> 00:00:59,040
That's when it can happen. Trust. Now it begins. The first page is always going to be the hardest,

12
00:00:59,040 --> 00:01:04,400
but it's really all about getting that ball rolling. Now that you've started, you have to

13
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:20,847
ask yourself the big scary fear question What am I doing wrong Be brutally honest As Quentin himself would say nail it Take your time Dive deep It gritty It tough But it absolutely necessary

14
00:01:20,847 --> 00:01:26,987
And when you push through, boom, you're halfway there.

15
00:01:26,987 --> 00:01:28,127
It's all out there.

16
00:01:28,127 --> 00:01:33,567
The fears, the doubts, the mistakes, the lessons, the heartbreak, all laid out bare for you

17
00:01:33,567 --> 00:01:34,707
to see.

18
00:01:34,707 --> 00:01:37,807
Not built up in your mind, but on paper.

19
00:01:37,807 --> 00:01:44,607
Take a moment, because now you have to ask yourself, how can I change it?

20
00:01:44,607 --> 00:01:46,587
We're not all Quentin Tarantino.

21
00:01:46,587 --> 00:01:48,907
You might be feeling like you're all written out.

22
00:01:48,907 --> 00:01:50,607
So let's make this part simple.

23
00:01:50,607 --> 00:01:52,207
A straightforward list.

24
00:01:52,207 --> 00:01:54,567
A hundred ways you can change your life.

25
00:01:54,567 --> 00:01:56,267
Quite a simple process.

26
00:01:56,267 --> 00:02:00,067
Take a mistake you've learned and write down a way to change it.

27
00:02:00,067 --> 00:02:03,367
Repeat it over and over again and push forward.

28
00:02:03,367 --> 00:02:04,367
Write it down.

29
00:02:04,367 --> 00:02:06,967
Adapt, reflect, learn and grow.

30
00:02:06,967 --> 00:02:10,407
And to finally, when you ask yourself, how can I change my life?

31
00:02:10,407 --> 00:02:12,067
You'll have a hundred ways to do it.

32
00:02:12,067 --> 00:02:15,667
But there's one very important thing you need to remember throughout this whole night.

33
00:02:15,667 --> 00:02:17,127
You gotta actually f***ing do it.
